@page "/Formula"
@using BlazorDatasheet.SharedPages.Components.Examples.Formula
<h3>Formula</h3>

<div class="block">
    BlazorDatasheet supports Excel formula. A subset of Excel formula functions have been implemented. Formula must start with '='.
</div>

<div class="block">
    Formula will automatically adjust references when rows or columns are inserted/deleted. Formula can use the $ syntax (as in Excel) which will keep references fixed when the auto-fill is used.
</div>

<CodeExample ComponentType="typeof(FormulaBasic)"/>

<h4 id="dynamic-arrays">Dynamic arrays</h4>

<div class="block">
    A formula whose result is an array <em>spills</em> into the cells below and to the right of it, as in Excel.
    Operators and functions that take a single value work element by element over a range or array,
    so <code>=A1:A6*2</code> fills six cells, and <code>=IF(A1:A6&gt;2,"high","low")</code> does too.
    The functions <code>SEQUENCE</code>, <code>TRANSPOSE</code>, <code>UNIQUE</code>, <code>SORT</code>,
    <code>SORTBY</code> and <code>FILTER</code> return arrays.
</div>

<div class="block">
    The cells a formula spills into cannot be edited; selecting one shows the formula in the formula bar and
    outlines the spill. If a cell in the way holds a value, a formula or a merge, the formula shows
    <code>#SPILL!</code> until the cell is cleared. <code>C1#</code> refers to whatever the formula in C1
    currently spills into, so <code>=SUM(C1#)</code> follows the spill as it grows and shrinks.
</div>

